; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR INVADERS  -  two rows of six, arrows to move, SPACE to fire
; ==========================================================================
; Two rows of six invaders march across the screen and drop a line each time they
; reach an edge. The gun sits on line 23. LEFT and RIGHT arrows move it, SPACE
; fires, and Esc (or Q) quits. If your terminal does not send arrow keys, a and d work too.
; One rocket in the air at a time. Shoot all twelve and you win; let them reach
; line 21 and they have landed.
;
; SHIP TABLE. The twelve ships are twelve bytes at $4960, one per ship - $01 alive,
; $00 destroyed - reached with READIDX and WRITEIDX, which index a
; program-relative base by a register and leave that register alone. Ships 0-5 are
; the top row, 6-11 the bottom.
;
; ONE DIVIDE ANSWERS "WHICH SHIP". Ships are three columns wide on a six-column
; pitch, so DIVXY of (rocket column - formation column) by six gives the ship
; number as the quotient and the offset within it as the remainder: a remainder of
; 0-2 is a hit, 3-5 is the gap between ships. The remainder is also exactly what
; the erase needs to find the ship's left-hand column, so it is kept in R11 rather
; than recomputed. An earlier draft divided a second time using a register that by
; then held the ship INDEX - which for ship 0 is a divide by zero, and that raises
; Error $07 and stops the VM.
;
; ARROW KEYS ARE THREE BYTES. The left arrow is ESC [ D and the right is ESC [ C,
; so a byte at a time is not enough - the program keeps a small state machine in
; memory at $4970: 0 = waiting for anything, 1 = seen ESC, 2 = seen ESC and [.
; So an ESC quits only on its own: nothing more within ~30 ms (the patches at $4300).
;
; DRAWING. The formation is redrawn only on the frames it actually marches - every
; eighth - not every frame. Redrawing it every frame costs about 110 bytes of
; output per frame and makes the ships shimmer; as it stands a quiet frame costs
; about 4 bytes. Each row is drawn as one 37-character run starting one column
; left of the formation, with dead ships drawn as blanks, so the same pass erases
; the trailing column and the destroyed ships without any separate erase.
;
; The gun is drawn with a space each side so a move wipes its own trail, and the
; rocket erases its old cell before drawing the new one.
;
; REGISTERS. R1 gun column, R2 rocket column, R3 rocket line (0 = none in flight),
; R4 formation column, R5 formation top line, R6 direction, R7 frame counter,
; R8 ships left, R9-R12 scratch, R13 line and R14 column for POSXY, R15 = ten.
; The end-of-game message is passed in R12 because R14 belongs to POSXY - passing
; it in R14 means the position call overwrites it, which is exactly the bug that
; made all three endings print YOU WIN.
;
; ADDRESSES. The LOADXI values in the code are PROGRAM-RELATIVE - $0960 means
; $4960 at run time, because MEMMODE is relative - but the data D-lines below carry
; the ABSOLUTE address. Writing the data at the relative address would drop the
; title text on top of the firmware: $09A0 is inside the opcode dispatch table.
;
; Sim-verified with an autoplayer driving the real key sequences: a full
; twelve-ship game played through to ALL SHIPS DESTROYED, the formation marching
; down to line 21 for THE INVADERS HAVE LANDED, Q for GAME ABANDONED, arrow keys
; and a/d both moving the gun, and ship 0 - the divide-by-zero case - destroyed
; cleanly.
;
; NOTE every D-line here is 16 bytes or fewer. The Elf2K monitor's input buffer is
; 64 characters - "D aaaa " plus 19 bytes - and it silently keeps what fits.
;
; 264 STELLAR commands, $4000-$42E7 (744 bytes of code).
; Plus the ESC patches at $4300-$4340 (2026-10-29), 21 commands.
; Data at $4900, 94 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $49A0, 30 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $49C0, 25 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $49E0, 15 bytes, past the end marker.
;
; ESC QUITS (2026-10-29): two patches past the end of the program, reached by GAL so no address moves.
; ESCW:
; D 4300 11 09 00 08    LOADXI R9 0008         ESC seen (state 1): is the rest of an arrow coming (~30 ms)?
; D 4304 CC             SERST
; D 4305 A0 01 0D       IFTRUEI NOKEY          yes: the state machine takes it
; D 4308 43 09          DECX R9
; D 430A 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 430C A1 03 04       IFFALSEI 4304
; D 430F B0 01 90       GAL QUIT               no: ESC on its own quits
; STARTK:
; D 4320 CB             SERIN                  The key that starts the game
; D 4321 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B            ESC?
; D 4324 A1 03 39       IFFALSEI GO
; D 4327 11 09 00 08    LOADXI R9 0008         an arrow following (~30 ms)?
; D 432B CC             SERST
; D 432C A0 03 39       IFTRUEI GO
; D 432F 43 09          DECX R9
; D 4331 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 4333 A1 03 2B       IFFALSEI 432B
; D 4336 B0 01 90       GAL QUIT               ESC on its own quits
; GO:
; D 4339 11 01 00 26    LOADXI R1 0026         Gun starts at column 38 (moved here from $4011)
; D 433D B0 00 15       GAL 4015               back to the game
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                  Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A        Ten, for splitting numbers into digits
; D 4005 11 0E 09 00    LOADXI R14 0900        Point at the title text
; D 4009 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14           Print it
; D 400B C3             RAND                   Stir the generator while we wait
; D 400C CC             SERST                  A key yet?
; D 400D A1 00 0B       IFFALSEI SEED
; D 4010 B0 03 20       GAL STARTK             Take the key (a lone ESC quits): the patch at $4320
; D 4013 C4 C4          NOP NOP                (not reached)
; D 4015 11 02 00 00    LOADXI R2 0000         No rocket in flight
; D 4019 11 03 00 00    LOADXI R3 0000
; D 401D 11 04 00 08    LOADXI R4 0008         The formation starts at column 8
; D 4021 11 05 00 02    LOADXI R5 0002         top row on line 2
; D 4025 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000         marching right
; D 4029 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000         Frame counter
; D 402D 11 08 00 0C    LOADXI R8 000C         Twelve ships to shoot down
; D 4031 11 0B 09 70    LOADXI R11 0970        Clear the arrow-key state
; D 4035 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000
; D 4039 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000         Ship index
; D 403D 10 00 01       LOADAI 0001            Alive
; D 4040 2F 09 09 60    WRITEIDX R9 0960
; D 4044 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4046 86 09 00 0C    TESTXI R9 000C         All twelve done?
; D 404A A1 00 3D       IFFALSEI MKALIVE
; D 404D CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ''
; D 404F CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             '['
; D 4051 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             '2'
; D 4053 CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A             'J'
; D 4055 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ''
; D 4057 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             '['
; D 4059 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             '?'
; D 405B CA 32          SEROUTI 32             '2'
; D 405D CA 35          SEROUTI 35             '5'
; D 405F CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C             'l'
; D 4061 BD 02 02       CALL DRAWALL           Both rows of ships
; D 4064 BD 01 BB       CALL DRAWGUN           and the gun
; D 4067 42 07          INCX R7                Count the frame
; D 4069 CC             SERST                  Anything typed?
; D 406A A1 01 0D       IFFALSEI NOKEY         No
; D 406D CB             SERIN                  Read the byte
; D 406E 21 0C          COPYAX 0C              Keep it in R12
; D 4070 11 0B 09 70    LOADXI R11 0970        Where are we in an escape sequence?
; D 4074 33 0B          COPYMXA 0B
; D 4076 81 00 01       TESTAI 0001            Waiting for the '[' ?
; D 4079 A0 00 B8       IFTRUEI KST1
; D 407C 33 0B          COPYMXA 0B
; D 407E 81 00 02       TESTAI 0002            Waiting for the letter?
; D 4081 A0 00 CA       IFTRUEI KST2
; D 4084 86 0C 00 1B    TESTXI R12 001B        ESC starts an arrow key
; D 4088 A1 00 92       IFFALSEI KNOTESC
; D 408B 32 0B 00 01    COPYMX2I R11 0001      Remember we have seen ESC
; D 408F B0 03 00       GAL ESCW               An arrow, or ESC on its own? (the patch at $4300)
; D 4092 86 0C 00 20    TESTXI R12 0020        Space fires
; D 4096 A0 00 FD       IFTRUEI FIRE
; D 4099 86 0C 00 71    TESTXI R12 0071        q quits
; D 409D A0 01 90       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 40A0 86 0C 00 51    TESTXI R12 0051        and so does Q
; D 40A4 A0 01 90       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 40A7 86 0C 00 61    TESTXI R12 0061        a moves left, for terminals that send no arrows
; D 40AB A0 00 DF       IFTRUEI GOLEFT
; D 40AE 86 0C 00 64    TESTXI R12 0064        d moves right
; D 40B2 A0 00 EE       IFTRUEI GORIGHT
; D 40B5 B0 01 0D       GAL NOKEY
; D 40B8 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000      Whatever it was, the sequence restarts
; D 40BC 86 0C 00 5B    TESTXI R12 005B        Was it '[' ?
; D 40C0 A1 01 0D       IFFALSEI NOKEY
; D 40C3 32 0B 00 02    COPYMX2I R11 0002      Now expect the letter
; D 40C7 B0 01 0D       GAL NOKEY
; D 40CA 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000      Sequence finished
; D 40CE 86 0C 00 44    TESTXI R12 0044        'D' is the left arrow
; D 40D2 A0 00 DF       IFTRUEI GOLEFT
; D 40D5 86 0C 00 43    TESTXI R12 0043        'C' is the right arrow
; D 40D9 A0 00 EE       IFTRUEI GORIGHT
; D 40DC B0 01 0D       GAL NOKEY
; D 40DF 86 01 00 02    TESTXI R1 0002         Already hard left?
; D 40E3 A0 01 0D       IFTRUEI NOKEY
; D 40E6 43 01          DECX R1
; D 40E8 BD 01 BB       CALL DRAWGUN
; D 40EB B0 01 0D       GAL NOKEY
; D 40EE 86 01 00 4D    TESTXI R1 004D         Already hard right? (column 77)
; D 40F2 A0 01 0D       IFTRUEI NOKEY
; D 40F5 42 01          INCX R1
; D 40F7 BD 01 BB       CALL DRAWGUN
; D 40FA B0 01 0D       GAL NOKEY
; D 40FD 8C 03          TESTXZ R3              Is a rocket already in flight?
; D 40FF A1 01 0D       IFFALSEI NOKEY         Yes - only one at a time
; D 4102 23 00 12       COPYXY R1 R2           It leaves from the gun
; D 4105 52 02 00 01    ADDXI R2 0001          from the middle of the barrel
; D 4109 11 03 00 16    LOADXI R3 0016         starting one line above the gun
; D 410D 8C 03          TESTXZ R3              Anything in flight?
; D 410F A0 01 37       IFTRUEI NOSHOT         No
; D 4112 23 00 3D       COPYXY R3 R13          Erase it from where it was
; D 4115 23 00 2E       COPYXY R2 R14
; D 4118 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 411B CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 411D 43 03          DECX R3                and move it up a line
; D 411F 8C 03          TESTXZ R3              Off the top of the screen?
; D 4121 A0 01 37       IFTRUEI NOSHOT         Then it is spent
; D 4124 BD 02 59       CALL HITTEST           Did it strike a ship?
; D 4127 8C 03          TESTXZ R3              HITTEST clears the rocket on a hit
; D 4129 A0 01 37       IFTRUEI NOSHOT
; D 412C 23 00 3D       COPYXY R3 R13          Draw it in its new place
; D 412F 23 00 2E       COPYXY R2 R14
; D 4132 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 4135 CA 7C          SEROUTI 7C             '|'
; D 4137 11 0B 00 08    LOADXI R11 0008
; D 413B 4D 7B          DIVXY R7 R11           Frame counter divided by eight
; D 413D 27             COPYREMA
; D 413E 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Is this a marching frame?
; D 4141 A1 01 71       IFFALSEI NOMARCH       No
; D 4144 86 06 00 00    TESTXI R6 0000         Marching right?
; D 4148 A1 01 5E       IFFALSEI MLEFT
; D 414B 42 04          INCX R4
; D 414D 86 04 00 2F    TESTXI R4 002F         Reached the right-hand limit? (column 47)
; D 4151 A1 01 6E       IFFALSEI MARCHED
; D 4154 11 06 00 01    LOADXI R6 0001         Turn around
; D 4158 BD 01 D5       CALL DROP              and drop a line
; D 415B B0 01 6E       GAL MARCHED
; D 415E 43 04          DECX R4
; D 4160 86 04 00 02    TESTXI R4 0002         Reached the left-hand limit?
; D 4164 A1 01 6E       IFFALSEI MARCHED
; D 4167 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000         Turn around
; D 416B BD 01 D5       CALL DROP              and drop a line
; D 416E BD 02 02       CALL DRAWALL           Redraw both rows - only on a marching frame
; D 4171 8C 08          TESTXZ R8              All twelve shot down?
; D 4173 A0 01 82       IFTRUEI WIN
; D 4176 86 05 00 15    TESTXI R5 0015         Has the formation reached line 21?
; D 417A A0 01 89       IFTRUEI LOSE
; D 417D C0 02          DLYI 02                Pace the game
; D 417F B0 00 67       GAL LOOP
; D 4182 11 0C 09 A0    LOADXI R12 09A0        The message goes in R12 - R14 is POSXY's column
; D 4186 B0 01 94       GAL FINISH
; D 4189 11 0C 09 C0    LOADXI R12 09C0
; D 418D B0 01 94       GAL FINISH
; D 4190 11 0C 09 E0    LOADXI R12 09E0
; D 4194 11 0D 00 0C    LOADXI R13 000C        Say so in the middle of the screen
; D 4198 11 0E 00 1A    LOADXI R14 001A
; D 419C BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 419F C1 0C          PRINTSTR R12           Whichever message we came here with
; D 41A1 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ''
; D 41A3 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             '['
; D 41A5 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             '?'
; D 41A7 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             '2'
; D 41A9 CA 35          SEROUTI 35             '5'
; D 41AB CA 68          SEROUTI 68             'h'
; D 41AD 11 0D 00 17    LOADXI R13 0017
; D 41B1 11 0E 00 01    LOADXI R14 0001
; D 41B5 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 41B8 F0 00 00       BREAK                  End of program
; D 41BB 11 0D 00 17    LOADXI R13 0017        Line 23
; D 41BF 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 R14
; D 41C2 52 0E FF FF    ADDXI R14 FFFF         one column to the left
; D 41C6 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 41C9 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 41CB CA 2F          SEROUTI 2F             '/'
; D 41CD CA 5E          SEROUTI 5E             '^'
; D 41CF CA 5C          SEROUTI 5C             '\'
; D 41D1 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 41D3 BE 00          RETURN
; D 41D5 23 00 5D       COPYXY R5 R13          Blank the two lines it is leaving
; D 41D8 BD 01 E9       CALL BLANKROW
; D 41DB 23 00 5D       COPYXY R5 R13
; D 41DE 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; D 41E2 BD 01 E9       CALL BLANKROW
; D 41E5 42 05          INCX R5
; D 41E7 BE 00          RETURN
; D 41E9 23 00 4E       COPYXY R4 R14
; D 41EC 52 0E FF FF    ADDXI R14 FFFF
; D 41F0 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 41F3 11 09 00 26    LOADXI R9 0026         38 columns
; D 41F7 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 41F9 43 09          DECX R9
; D 41FB 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 41FD A1 01 F7       IFFALSEI BLLOOP
; D 4200 BE 00          RETURN
; D 4202 23 00 5D       COPYXY R5 R13          Top row
; D 4205 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000        ships 0-5
; D 4209 BD 02 1C       CALL DRAWROW
; D 420C 23 00 5D       COPYXY R5 R13          Bottom row, two lines down
; D 420F 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; D 4213 11 0B 00 06    LOADXI R11 0006        ships 6-11
; D 4217 BD 02 1C       CALL DRAWROW
; D 421A BE 00          RETURN
; D 421C 23 00 4E       COPYXY R4 R14
; D 421F 52 0E FF FF    ADDXI R14 FFFF         start one column left, to wipe the trailing edge
; D 4223 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 4226 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 4228 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000         Ship number within the row
; D 422C 50 B9 0A       ADDXYZ R11 R9 R10      Index into the alive table
; D 422F 2E 0A 09 60    READIDX R10 0960       Is this one still flying?
; D 4233 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4236 A0 02 42       IFTRUEI DRDEAD         No - leave a hole
; D 4239 CA 3C          SEROUTI 3C             '<'
; D 423B CA 4F          SEROUTI 4F             'O'
; D 423D CA 3E          SEROUTI 3E             '>'
; D 423F B0 02 48       GAL DRGAP
; D 4242 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 4244 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 4246 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 4248 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 424A CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 424C CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 424E 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4250 86 09 00 06    TESTXI R9 0006         All six done?
; D 4254 A1 02 2C       IFFALSEI DRLOOP
; D 4257 BE 00          RETURN
; D 4259 23 00 5B       COPYXY R5 R11          The top row's line
; D 425C 87 3B          TESTXY R3 R11          Is the rocket on it?
; D 425E A0 02 71       IFTRUEI HTROW0
; D 4261 52 0B 00 02    ADDXI R11 0002         The bottom row's line
; D 4265 87 3B          TESTXY R3 R11
; D 4267 A1 02 C4       IFFALSEI HTNONE        Neither - nothing to hit
; D 426A 11 0C 00 06    LOADXI R12 0006        Ships 6-11 are the bottom row
; D 426E B0 02 75       GAL HTCOL
; D 4271 11 0C 00 00    LOADXI R12 0000        Ships 0-5
; D 4275 88 24          TESTGXY R2 R4          Is the rocket right of the formation's left edge?
; D 4277 A1 02 C4       IFFALSEI HTNONE
; D 427A 51 24 0B       SUBXYZ R2 R4 R11       How far into the formation
; D 427D 11 0A 00 06    LOADXI R10 0006        Six columns per ship
; D 4281 4D BA          DIVXY R11 R10          One divide gives both answers
; D 4283 27             COPYREMA               The remainder is the offset within the ship
; D 4284 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Keep it in R11 - the erase below needs it
; D 4286 25             COPYMAA                and the quotient is which ship in the row
; D 4287 21 09          COPYAX 09
; D 4289 88 9A          TESTGXY R9 R10         Past the sixth ship?
; D 428B A0 02 C4       IFTRUEI HTNONE         Then it is beyond the formation
; D 428E 11 0A 00 03    LOADXI R10 0003        A ship is three columns wide
; D 4292 88 BA          TESTGXY R11 R10        Is the rocket in the gap between ships?
; D 4294 A0 02 C4       IFTRUEI HTNONE         Yes - a clean miss
; D 4297 50 C9 0A       ADDXYZ R12 R9 R10      The ship's index in the alive table
; D 429A 2E 0A 09 60    READIDX R10 0960       Is it still there?
; D 429E 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 42A1 A0 02 C4       IFTRUEI HTNONE         Already destroyed
; D 42A4 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000            Mark it destroyed
; D 42A7 2F 0A 09 60    WRITEIDX R10 0960
; D 42AB 43 08          DECX R8                One fewer ship
; D 42AD 23 00 3D       COPYXY R3 R13          Wipe the ship off the screen
; D 42B0 51 2B 0E       SUBXYZ R2 R11 R14      R11 still holds the offset, so this is the ship's left column
; D 42B3 BD 02 C6       CALL POSXY
; D 42B6 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 42B8 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 42BA CA 20          SEROUTI 20             ' '
; D 42BC 11 03 00 00    LOADXI R3 0000         The rocket is spent
; D 42C0 11 02 00 00    LOADXI R2 0000
; D 42C4 BE 00          RETURN
; D 42C6 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ''
; D 42C8 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             '['
; D 42CA 4D DF          DIVXY R13 R15
; D 42CC 25             COPYMAA
; D 42CD 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 42D0 C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 42D1 27             COPYREMA
; D 42D2 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 42D5 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 42D6 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B             ';'
; D 42D8 4D EF          DIVXY R14 R15
; D 42DA 25             COPYMAA
; D 42DB 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 42DE C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 42DF 27             COPYREMA
; D 42E0 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 42E3 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 42E4 CA 48          SEROUTI 48             'H'
; D 42E6 BE 00          RETURN
